# What the Linux Flatpak (packaging/flatpak) installs into its sandbox, besides what the GNOME runtime already has
# (Python 3.12, PyGObject, WebKitGTK): Hoard's own dependencies and its window (pywebview, which uses the runtime's
# WebKitGTK). requirements-flatpak.txt is generated from this for Linux x86_64 and Python 3.12, with hashes:
#   uv pip compile requirements-flatpak.in -c requirements.txt -c requirements-app.txt --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 \
#     --python-version 3.12 --generate-hashes --no-header --output-file requirements-flatpak.txt
# then packaging/flatpak/python3-deps.json with:  python scripts/flatpak_deps.py
# (-c: the same versions as a source install and the Windows app.)
# Don't edit either by hand; change this file (or requirements.in) and regenerate them.
-r requirements.in
pywebview>=5.3,<7
